{"author":"schacon@gmail.com","body":"When checking out a ticket (ti checkout), automatically create or switch to a git branch named after the ticket (e.g. ti/a3f-fix-the-parser). When on a ticket branch, ti commands default to that ticket without needing explicit checkout state.\n\nFeatures:\n- ti checkout <id> creates/switches to a branch (e.g. ti/a3f-fix-the-parser)\n- ti commands auto-detect current ticket from branch name\n- ti new --branch immediately creates and switches to the ticket branch\n- Configurable branch naming pattern (ti/<id>-<slug>, ticket/<id>, etc)\n- Store branch association in ticket metadata (code field or meta:branch)\n- ti list --branch to show which tickets have active branches"}